PATCH 405: editor REMOVE-TANK edit-op harness (env-gated FIST_EDIT_REMTANK, DEFAULT OFF).

The THIRD editor DoD deliverable, the inverse of patch 362's add-tank: drive one DELETE op (REMOVE
TANK) -> save -> verify the delta.  Like patches 361/362 this is an env-gated harness hook in the
ACCEPT cascade FUN_0000_4754, fired right after FUN_0000_d501 has LOADED the selected battle into the
battle-state DGROUP + the live unit registry, and BEFORE FUN_1000_6015 / the e4bb game loop.  With
FIST_EDIT_REMTANK set it:
  1. enters EDITING mode faithfully (DAT_2000_2dab |= 2, the bit2=EDITING flag);
  2. finds the first loaded FRIENDLY unit in the 0x9fbc registry (team bit byte[obj-0x19ec]&1 == 0,
     the same probe patch 362 uses to pick the clone source), then
  3. DESTROYS it through the engine's REAL object-destroy method FUN_1000_b2ef (patch 363) -- which
     marks byte[obj+0x16]|=1, clears the 0x9fbc registry slot, decrements the 0x9fbe count, and removes
     the roster presence flag + count (a2f7/a294 friendly or a38d/a296 enemy), exactly the state the
     DCBS serializer d6e4 walks;
  4. drives the engine's OWN serializer FUN_0000_d5f9 to save, and exits.

This is the FIRST exercise of patch 363's b2ef.  The serialized DCBS has ONE FEWER unit (base ->
base-1), it RELOADS, and load->save on the edited file is an idempotent FIXED POINT -- verified native
AND wasm, native==wasm 0-diff, over a theatre spread of battles (see tools/verify.sh editor-rem-tank-*).

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -14078,16 +14078,39 @@
           if (fbc[f * 2] == 0 && fbc[f * 2 + 1] == 0) break;
         fbc[f * 2] = nrec; fbc[f * 2 + 1] = val;            /* register the new unit -> counted + saved */
         FUN_1000_66cd(0xd27);                               /* editor status: "TANK ADDED" */
       }
     }
     FUN_0000_d5f9(0,0,0,0x79a9,0,0);                        /* save via the reconstructed serializer */
     exit(0);
   }
+  if (getenv("FIST_EDIT_REMTANK")) {
+    /* PATCH 405: editor REMOVE-TANK edit-op harness (env-gated FIST_EDIT_REMTANK, DEFAULT OFF ->
+       behaviour-neutral for verify).  Mirror of patch 362's add-tank, driving the engine's REAL
+       object-DESTROY method b2ef (patch 363): after d501 LOADS the battle and BEFORE 6015, enter
+       EDITING mode, find the first loaded FRIENDLY unit in the 0x9fbc registry, and destroy it via
+       FUN_1000_b2ef(k) -- which clears the 0x9fbc slot, decrements the 0x9fbe count, and removes the
+       roster presence flag + count (a2f7/a294 friendly or a38d/a296 enemy).  Then drive the serializer
+       d5f9 and exit.  The serialized DCBS has ONE FEWER unit (base -> base-1); verified by reload +
+       idempotent fixed point, exactly like add-tank.  First exercise of patch 363's b2ef. */
+    unsigned char *dg = (unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000;
+    unsigned short *fbc = (unsigned short *)(dg + 0xdfbc);   /* 0x9fbc unit registry {slot,val} x0xb6 */
+    int k;
+    DAT_2000_2dab = DAT_2000_2dab | 2;                       /* enter EDITING mode (2dab bit2 = EDIT) */
+    for (k = 0; k < 0xb6; k = k + 1) {                       /* first FRIENDLY loaded unit (team bit 0) */
+      unsigned short s = fbc[k * 2];
+      if (s != 0) {
+        unsigned short obj = *(unsigned short *)(dg + s);
+        if ((dg[(unsigned short)(obj - 0x19ec)] & 1) == 0) { FUN_1000_b2ef(k); break; }
+      }
+    }
+    FUN_0000_d5f9(0,0,0,0x79a9,0,0);                        /* save via the reconstructed serializer */
+    exit(0);
+  }
   if (!(bool)in_CF) {
     FUN_1000_6015();
     DAT_2000_39a8 = 1;
   }
   return;
 }
 
 
